# OpenMW Analytics — world placement survey (BUILD STEP, design docs 11 §13)
#
# ⚠️ DO NOT add this to your normal profile. It is deliberately a SEPARATE content file so the
# survey CANNOT run during ordinary play.
#
# The survey must run against a CONTROLLED load order — Morrowind.esm + Tribunal.esm +
# Bloodmoon.esm + the measured mod + omwanalytics, and nothing else — because Lua cannot report an
# object's provenance. Run on a modded setup it would silently bake hundreds of personal mods'
# placements into a corpus meant to describe the shared base.
#
# The ingest REFUSES a manifest whose load order fails the allowlist, so a contaminated survey
# cannot reach the database. This file existing separately is the first line of that defence; the
# refusal is the second.
#
# Usage: point OpenMW at a second config containing only the controlled load order, add
#   content=omwanalytics-survey.omwscripts
# launch, load any save, wait for the OMWAS1 footer line in openmw.log, quit.
GLOBAL: scripts/omwanalytics/survey.lua
